{
  "_readme": [
    "One file to swap draft visuals for real captures. No component edits needed.",
    "",
    "Every scene reads its screen source from here. `source: null` means the scene",
    "uses the `stills` map (real simulator screenshots) or remains a designed board.",
    "Hook, Problem and Close are always designed; the other six accept a source.",
    "Replace a scene by setting its `source`:",
    "  { \"kind\": \"clip\",   \"src\": \"clips/auth.mp4\", \"delay\": 1.1 }",
    "  { \"kind\": \"frames\", \"dir\": \"clips/auth\", \"fps\": 9.91, \"count\": 182 }",
    "    optional: \"meta\": \"clips/auth/meta.json\", \"timeline\": \"clips/timeline.json\"",
    "Files must live under demo/film/public/. Use `npm run sync-recordings` after new captures.",
    "",
    "`inputs` are ring-gesture overlays, in seconds from the scene start. They are",
    "generated from each recording's timeline by `npm run sync-recordings`; do not",
    "hand-edit them or add an input the recording does not contain.",
    "`status` is the honesty label reported in the render summary and shown in the",
    "top-right proof tag. Change it when a placeholder becomes a real capture.",
    "",
    "Scene timings live in src/pinpoint/timeline.ts (140 s total, 30 fps)."
  ],
